<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. UFR reviewed by AC and approved by BoD on 13.08.2024. Statutory Auditors have conducted limited review of unaudited FR.   2. FR prepared as per Ind-AS u/s 133 of Co. Act, 2013 read with Co. (Ind AS) Rules, 2015.   3. Fig for the qtr ended 31.03.2024 represents derived fig. b/w audited fig. for relevant FY and unaud. yr to date fig. upto 31st Dec, date of end of 3rd qtr of relevant FY subjected to ltd review by stat aud.   4. RB vide CC60 of 2019 reg. inc. in catg tariff for post and pre-paid trains. Effect of inc. of License Fee from 18.11.2019 to 22.03 2020 (for postpaid trains) and 27.11.2021 to 31.12.2023 (for post and prepaid trains) has not been recog. as some of licensees have challenged Co. decision in resp. High Courts of Delhi, Mumbai, Kolkata and Guwahati &amp; arbitration. As matter is sub-judice &amp; occurrence is dependent on outcome of certain event in future, the impact of increase in License fees for trains not recognized in FS for quarter 30.06.2024 and for PYs up to 31.03.2024.   5. Upto FY 23, Co. provided Rly. share @15% on pft of RN for plants run departmentally as well as plants run on PPP. During FY24, RB advised, Co. provided Railway share @15% on departmentally run Railneer plants and 40% on PPP plants. Prov. for differential amount of profit sharing  @25% (40%-15%) upto 31.03.2023 have been made for Rs.1451.24 Lakhs during FY24 &amp; shown as exceptional item in FR for 31.03.2024, even though Co. represented for sharing at 15:85 for all RN plants till FY23. Response from RB awaited.   6. As per T&amp;C of tender, for 4 PPP RN plants, DCOs to be reimbursed GST on sales (net of ITC) availed by them. In absence of info of ITC availed by DCOs, Rs.98.36 L has been accounted during quarter ended 30.06.2024 and Rs.364.83 L for FY24. DCOs represented against the claim for ITC. Being examined by the Mgt.   7. NAA issued notice dt 25.02.22 for profiteering amount of Rs.5041.44 L u/s 171 of CGST Act for not passing benefit of tax reduction to consumers. CCI empowered to adjudicate the matter. Proceedings stands concluded and, if any, to be commenced afresh by CCI &amp; as on date no comm. received from CCI.   8. Certain Licensees invoked arbitration for compensation of diff. rates of regular &amp; combo meal provided under CCs issued by IR and claimed price of welcome drink from 2014 till date. Arbitrator awarded Rs.7471.65 L (approx.) in 13 petitions from Jan 2015 to Mar 2020. On record claimant never claimed said amount while submitting invoices for services rendered. Services provided to passengers of IR &amp; amt. so paid is req. to be reimbursed to IRCTC by IR. In this case, no liability of IRCTC as conseq. of award &amp; no need to make prov. pursuant to awards. Co. filed objection &amp; Hon’ble HC, Delhi directed Co. to deposit amt. to stay execution of Arbitral Award. Deposited a BG to tune of Rs.8471.65 L to stay execution of said award. Hon’ble HC, Delhi has reserved the judgment.   9. a) For qtr ended 30.06.2024, Exceptional items represent Rs.220.72 L towards reversal of RU, Stabling &amp; other charges waived off on GC train by KTDC for pr. FY 23 &amp; 24.    (b) For PY FY24, net expense on account of Exceptional items amounting Rs.5853.03 L includes: (i) Rs.5126.20 L being prov. made towards revised fixed, variable &amp; Custody charges for 2 Tejas trains w.e.f. 13.08.21 to 31.03.23 in line with letter received from MOR even though Co. made rep. to RB for waiver amount, (ii)Rs 1451.24 L being provision made twd diff. amt. of profit sharing  @25% (40%-15%)  up to 31.03.2023 on profits of RN plants operated on PPP model and (iii) Rs.724.41 L being excess prov. written back for PY relating to exp..   10. Fig. for PY/periods regrouped/reclassified/restated.   11. Subs. Co. was inc. on 10.02.2024 &amp; did not exist during 30.06.23 &amp; hence, fig. for qtr ended 30.06.2023 pertain to parent co.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
